From 015a870ad79dfd037db167edca0ed49d072aa8fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcin <91057909+mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:41:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GBM] Update the resolutions on display hotplug

A display that is asleep when Kodi starts may return no EDID, leaving
only the fallback modes like 1024x768. When it wakes up, the kernel
reads the EDID and sends a hotplug uevent, but GBM never asked for the
connector again and stayed on the fallback modes until a restart.

Watch the drm uevents and probe the connector once the hotplugs settle.
A probe without an EDID is ignored, so a display going to sleep keeps
its modes. A new EDID updates the display info. If the modes changed,
update the resolutions and apply the one from the settings again.
A playing video and open modal dialogs are left alone until they end.
